00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.440
Universe today reports that researchers at Cornell and the University of Bristol found

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.100
strong evening side winds and blistering temperatures on one face.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.120
Infrared data resolve distinct regions instead of averaging light from the whole disc.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.860
Phase curve measurements tracked how the planets light changed as it circled its star.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.800
The world is not uniform with different temperatures and winds from one side to the other.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:44.020
