00:04:41.196 --> 00:04:46.816
Deep in Earth's mantle, right above the core, a large share of the rock is magnesium oxide crystals.

00:04:47.436 --> 00:04:52.476
They sit under pressure roughly 1.3 million times the atmospheric pressure at the surface.

00:04:53.196 --> 00:05:00.416
Fizz.org reports that on larger rocky worlds called super-Earths, those same crystals would feel pressures several times higher.

00:05:00.416 --> 00:05:05.756
That extra squeeze can force the material into a new atomic arrangement, or turn it into

00:05:05.756 --> 00:05:06.436
a liquid metal.

00:05:07.116 --> 00:05:08.316
The change is not gradual.

00:05:08.996 --> 00:05:13.776
Once pressure crosses a threshold, the crystal lattice collapses and the atoms settle into

00:05:13.776 --> 00:05:15.436
a structure that conducts electricity.

00:05:16.256 --> 00:05:21.296
Lab work that crushes tiny samples between diamond anvils already puts that transition inside

00:05:21.296 --> 00:05:25.516
the pressure range expected in planets only a few times more massive than Earth.

00:05:25.516 --> 00:05:31.496
A metallic liquid like that could drive magnetic fields by dynamo-action, something ordinary

00:05:31.496 --> 00:05:33.256
magnesium oxide cannot do.

00:05:33.756 --> 00:05:38.936
The same process may run in the cores of gas giants, where magnesium oxide could sit in

00:05:38.936 --> 00:05:40.436
metallic form even deeper.

00:05:41.136 --> 00:05:45.916
No one yet knows how much of a planet's interior must convert before a global magnetic field

00:05:45.916 --> 00:05:46.236
appears.

00:05:46.916 --> 00:05:51.956
It is also unclear whether the transition builds stable layers that block convection, or

00:05:51.956 --> 00:05:52.876
layers that help it.

00:05:52.876 --> 00:05:58.256
Atoms under that crust shift into arrangements that let electrons move freely, turning an

00:05:58.256 --> 00:05:59.656
insulator into a conductor.

00:06:00.096 --> 00:06:05.196
That is one way some planets could keep strong magnetic fields while others do not, even

00:06:05.196 --> 00:06:07.716
when size and makeup look similar from the outside.

00:06:08.396 --> 00:06:12.936
The exact pressure where magnesium oxide turns metallic is still a number models have

00:06:12.936 --> 00:06:13.636
to pin down.

00:06:14.216 --> 00:06:18.616
Until that threshold is measured under conditions that match real planetary interiors,

00:06:18.616 --> 00:06:23.356
Forecasts about which exoplanets host global magnetic shields will stay uncertain.

